  "description": "The HTTP request each REST operation must produce, and what it returns for a given response. All cases use restEndpoint http://node.test and, unless stated, key ck_test_5f2c8a1e9b.k25b5a4. Channel names go into the path percent-encoded so that they decode back to the exact name: a space is %20 and never +, a slash is %2F, a colon may be sent raw or as %3A. `path` is what encodeURIComponent yields; an SDK passes if its path percent-decodes to `pathDecoded`, contains no + and no raw / inside the channel segment. Header values are true (must be present and equal the top-level `authorization`, or the stated content type) or false (must be absent). Bodies are compared as parsed JSON, not as text; keys listed in `bodyNullableKeys` may be absent or null.",
